.TH "GLESHA-UNDELETE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-undelete \- restore sets from the trash
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha undelete\fR SET... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take each SET out of the trash before its trash period ends and before its deletion starts. Nothing was deleted, so the set is restored exactly.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha undelete docs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1)
